cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "Agent Memory Below the Prompt: Persistent Q4 KV Cache for Multi-Agent LLM Inference on Edge Devices"
authors:
  - family-names: Shkolnikov
    given-names: Yakov Pyotr
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-03-29
license: MIT
url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.04428"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.18793752"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yshk-mxim/agent-memory"
abstract: "Multi-agent LLM systems on edge devices face a memory management problem: device RAM is too small to hold every agent's KV cache simultaneously. We address this by persisting each agent's KV cache to disk in 4-bit quantized format and reloading it directly into the attention layer, eliminating redundant prefill computation. Evaluated on Gemma 3 12B, DeepSeek-Coder-V2-Lite 16B, and Llama 3.1 8B, cache restoration reduces time-to-first-token by up to 136x."
keywords:
  - kv-cache
  - multi-agent
  - llm-inference
  - edge-computing
  - apple-silicon
  - nvidia-jetson
  - tensorrt
  - quantization
